title="Local Kato Theory for the Incompressible Navier–Stokes Equations on ℝ³, Kernel-Checked in Lean 4: A Maximal Solution with an H³ Blow-up Alternative for ν > 0 (Not Global Regularity; Not Fefferman's Problem (A))"
desc="""<p><strong>Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Stanley Frohman.</strong> Paper: CC BY 4.0. Lean code: Apache-2.0.</p>
<p><strong>What is proved (kernel-checked).</strong> For every viscosity ν &gt; 0 and every smooth, divergence-free initial field u₀ on ℝ³ satisfying Fefferman's decay condition (4), the Lean 4 proposition <code>KatoMaximalSolution ν u₀</code> holds (<code>KatoMaximal.katoMaximalSolution_of_feffermanDecay</code>): there exist a time set S, a velocity u, a pressure p and a constant C_k ≥ 0 such that (i) (u, p) is a smooth Navier–Stokes solution from u₀ in the class <code>IsFeffermanSolutionOn</code> on every [0, T) ⊆ S; (ii) ‖u(t)‖²_{H³} is finite on S, continuous on S, and at every s ∈ S has a right derivative d ≤ C_k ‖∇u(s)‖_∞ ‖u(s)‖²_{H³}; (iii) either S = [0, ∞), or S = [0, T*) with T* &gt; 0 and ‖u(t)‖²_{H³} unbounded on S. The paper also quotes the kernel-checked properties of the realized maximal solution on its maximal time set (Kato–Ponce H³ bound, vanishing-flux package, Fefferman-class solution on every [0,T) ⊆ S_max, momentum equation, energy inequality, continuity of the H³ energy, H³ blow-up alternative, shape of S_max).</p>
<p><strong>Conditional statements.</strong> <code>KatoContinuation.r3BKMContinuation_of_pos</code> proves <code>R3BKMContinuation ν</code> for ν &gt; 0; that proposition keeps a uniform ‖ω‖_∞ ceiling along local solutions as a hypothesis. <code>KatoContinuation.clay_A_fefferman_of_rate</code> derives <code>Clay_A_Fefferman</code> from <code>FrohmanianTetherRateSmooth</code> for all Fefferman data; that hypothesis is not proved.</p>
<p><strong>Scope.</strong> This is local Kato theory. It is not a global regularity theorem, it does not prove Fefferman's Problem (A), and it does not solve any open problem.</p>
<p><strong>Certificate.</strong> Every Lean statement is quoted verbatim from <code>Scratch/KatoMaximal.lean</code> and <code>Scratch/KatoContinuation.lean</code> of <a href="https://github.com/BenFrohman/frohmanian-tether-sdiff/tree/ad546216d56b5ab7514f1ed20fe168744ff9cf74">BenFrohman/frohmanian-tether-sdiff</a> at commit <code>ad546216d56b5ab7514f1ed20fe168744ff9cf74</code> (merge of pull request #12). Built by <code>lake build</code> and <code>lake build Scratch</code> on GitHub Actions run <a href="https://github.com/BenFrohman/frohmanian-tether-sdiff/actions/runs/44042177446">44042177446</a> (success) with the repository's own <code>lake-manifest.json</code> (sha256 7d1ab35f9874f0c261e99ae06fe05446a8cec85dd4c9af79b016b73032bc0955), toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.30.0-rc1, Lake 5.0.0-src+714601b, Mathlib v4.30.0-rc1 (0c154d67103f74be3a0f2c509f72ccbf5be9f2a7). <code>#print axioms</code> reports [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] for each main theorem; no sorryAx. The certificate bundle contains the pinned manifest, toolchain and lakefile, and the unmodified GitHub run logs and artifacts of runs 44042177446, 44042177503 (Kernel certificate) and 44042177638 (truth-gate), with SHA256SUMS. The elan version is not recorded by these runs.</p>
<p>Rebuild: <code>git clone https://github.com/BenFrohman/frohmanian-tether-sdiff.git &amp;&amp; cd frohmanian-tether-sdiff &amp;&amp; git checkout ad546216d56b5ab7514f1ed20fe168744ff9cf74 &amp;&amp; bash scripts/verify.sh &amp;&amp; lake build Scratch &amp;&amp; lake env lean scripts/PrintScratchAxioms.lean</code></p>
<p>Please cite this work and credit Benjamin Stanley Frohman (ORCID 0009-0006-7068-3718); see NOTICE.</p>"""
